        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenneth Anderson, Dwight D. Eisenhower\n- Roles: British Army officer, American politician, Army general, President of the United States\n\nFacts:\n- Dwight D. Eisenhower was born on October 14, 1890, and died on March 28, 1969.\n- Dwight D. Eisenhower was an American politician and Army general.\n- Dwight D. Eisenhower served as the 34th President of the United States from 1953 to 1961.\n- Kenneth Anderson was a British Army officer.\n- Dwight D. Eisenhower was Kenneth Anderson's American superior.\n- Dwight D. Eisenhower wrote that Kenneth Anderson was \"blunt, at times to the point of rudeness\".",
